LINKING EXCEPTION
=================

As a special exception, the copyright holders of Stellurgy give you
permission to link or combine independent modules with Stellurgy solely
through its public API — the `dev.stannismod.stellurgy.api` package and its
subpackages — to produce a combined work, and to convey the resulting combined
work under terms of your choice, provided that:

  (a) the independent module uses Stellurgy only through that public
      API, and is not otherwise derived from or based on Stellurgy; and

  (b) you comply with the GNU General Public License, version 3, for Stellurgy
      itself and for any modifications you make to it.

An "independent module" is a module which is not derived from or based on
Stellurgy other than through the public API named above. Depending on,
linking against, or calling that public API does not, by itself, make your work
a work based on Stellurgy for the purposes of this License.

If you modify Stellurgy itself — any code outside the public API named
above — this exception does not extend to those modifications, which remain
governed by the GNU General Public License, version 3.

You may, at your option, remove this exception from a given copy of the program;
doing so makes the plain GNU General Public License, version 3, apply to that
copy.


